## Works Modal & SCSS Structure — Complete Exploration Report

### 1. **Works Modal TypeScript/JavaScript Files**

**Main Modal Component:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/ui/WorkModal.ts`
  - Class: `WorkModal extends UI`
  - Key methods: `runOpenByNo()`, `_openByEndpoint()`, `_fetchModal()`, `_show()`, `_hide()`
  - Handles modal opening/closing, debouncing, scroll lock, and backdrop interaction
  - Uses `fetchWorksModalHtml()` API to fetch modal content dynamically

**Works Page Runtime Files:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/works/runtime/WorksPageRuntime.ts` — Main page state management
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/works/runtime/WorksIntroRuntime.ts` — Intro overlay logic
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/works/scene/works.scene.ts` — Scene configuration and constants
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/works/render/WorksSceneManager.ts` — Three.js rendering
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/ts/pages/works/theatre/` — Theatre.js animation bridge and config

### 2. **Works-Related SCSS/CSS Files**

**Modal Styling:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/scss/components/_modal.scss` (241 lines)
  - Class: `.no-work-modal` — BEM structure for modal component
  - Subclasses: `__backdrop`, `__shell`, `__panel`, `__thumbnail`, `__content`, `__header`, `__title`, `__info`, `__close`, `__award`, `__button`
  - Uses `fluid()` function for responsive sizing
  - State classes: `.is-open`, `.is-closing`
  - Includes transitions and animations with `var(--modal-enter-ease)`

**Works Canvas/Grid View Styling:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/scss/pages/_works-canvas.scss` (548 lines)
  - Class: `.no-works-canvas` — Main container for scatter/grid view
  - Includes filter button, view toggle, pagination controls
  - Keyframes: `@keyframes works-filter-label-in`, `@keyframes works-drag-hint-icon-bell`
  - Responsive breakpoints: `@include mq(md)` (768px), `@include mq(sm)` (544px)

**Works Detail View Styling:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/resource/scss/pages/_sub.scss` (lines 1822–1985)
  - Class: `.no-sub-work-view` — Detail page layout
  - Responsive breakpoints: `@include mq(md)`, `@include mq(sm)`
  - Grid layout: `grid-template-columns: 10fr 2fr` (desktop), adapts on mobile

### 3. **Responsive Breakpoint Patterns**

**Container Size Tokens** (in `_variables.scss`):
```scss
$containers: (
  3xl: 1920,   // max-width desktop
  2xl: 1640,
  xl: 1440,
  lg: 1024,
  md: 768,     // tablet & landscape phone
  sm: 544,     // mobile
  xs: 375,     // small mobile
);
```

**Mixin Usage:**
- `@include mq($key-or-size, $direction: "max")` — Media query helper
- `@include mq-max(key)` — `max-width` breakpoint (default, mobile-first)
- `@include mq-min(key)` — `min-width` breakpoint
- Example: `@include mq(md)` = `@media (max-width: 768px) { ... }`

**Responsive Patterns Found in Works:**

Works Canvas responsive:
```scss
@include mq(md) {
  &__bottom-controls {
    width: calc(100vw - fluid(24, 32));
    max-width: fluid(340, 420);
  }
}

@include mq(sm) {
  &__bottom-toggle {
    @include font("f-body-5");
  }
}
```

Works Detail View responsive:
```scss
&__info {
  grid-template-columns: 10fr 2fr;  // desktop

  &-list {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);  // 4 column grid
  }
}

@include mq(md) {
  &__info {
    grid-template-columns: 1fr;  // single column on tablet
  }

  &__info-list {
    grid-template-columns: repeat(4, 1fr);  // but 4-col list items
  }
}

@include mq(sm) {
  // single column for everything
}
```

**Fluid Typography System:**
- `@function fluid($min, $max, $x1: 375, $x2: 1920)` — CSS `clamp()` for responsive sizing
- `@include font("f-heading-1")` — Uses fluid typography maps
- `@include fs-fluid($min, $max)` — Direct fluid font sizing

### 4. **Works View PHP Blade Files**

**Main Works View Page:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/views/pages/works/view.php` (175 lines)
  - Structure: header (title + award), info section (service, client, category, update), thumbnail (video/image), content (overview + contents), detail images
  - Uses `include_view('components.work-modal', ['work' => $work])` for modal rendering
  - Includes "Visit Website" and "Go To List" buttons
  - Returns to works list with query params (view, category, page)

**Works Modal Component:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/views/components/work-modal.php` (133 lines)
  - Root: `<div class="no-work-modal" data-work-modal-root role="dialog">`
  - Nested structure: backdrop, shell (close button), panel (header, info, thumbnail, content)
  - Info items: SERVICE (multi-value list), CLIENT, CATEGORY, UPDATE
  - Content sections: OVERVIEW, CONTENTS, detail image gallery

**Modal Entry Page:**
- `/c/Users/edn_y/renew_nineonelabs/views/pages/works/modal.php` (29 lines)
  - Wrapper page for `/works/modal-component/{no}` endpoint
  - Renders modal component via `include_view('components.work-modal')`

### 5. **Existing Responsive CSS in Works Modal**

**Modal Panel** (`_modal.scss` lines 24–61):
```scss
&__shell {
  position: relative;
  width: min(100%, fluid(544, 1024));  // responsive width
  max-height: 76vh;  // max height
}

&__panel {
  transform: translate3d(0, fluid(48, 72), 0) scale(0.985);  // entry animation
  max-height: 76vh;
  overflow-y: auto;
}
```

**Modal Close Button:**
```scss
&__close {
  width: fluid(36, 40);  // responsive button size
  height: fluid(36, 40);
  top: fluid(16, 24);
  right: fluid(16, 24);
}
```

**Award Badge:**
```scss
&__award {
  img {
    width: fluid(20, 36);  // responsive icon
    height: fluid(20, 36);
  }
}
```

**Info Section:**
```scss
&__info {
  display: flex;
  justify-content: space-between;

  &-item {
    grid-template-columns: fluid(84, 120) 1fr;  // label + content responsive
    gap: var(--gutter-sm);
  }
}
```

**No explicit mobile-specific media queries in modal — relies on fluid() function and padding variables.**

### 6. **CSS Architecture Summary**

- **Entry:** `resource/scss/style.scss` (uses CSS Cascade Layers)
- **Layer order:** reset → base → layout → components → pages → utilities → state
- **Abstract tokens:** `resource/scss/abstract/` (colors, variables, mixins, functions)
- **Token contract:** Use semantic vars (`var(--clr-*`, `var(--gutter-*`, `var(--duration-*)`) not raw hex
- **Compiled output:** `resource/dist/style.css` (dev server auto-builds on save)
- **Fluid sizing:** Primary responsive strategy via `clamp()` function
- **Media queries:** `mq()` mixin for container-based breakpoints
- **Min/max approach:** Defaults to `max-width` (mobile-first, then desktop overrides)

